course: dictionary
lesson: 6314
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one job. A mosquito is a small flying insect, and the females bite people and animals to suck their blood. The words around the word show which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «Spiders in homes eat flies, mosquitoes and other pests.» Here mosquitoes are food for spiders, so the sentence tells you they are small and easy to catch. Ask yourself: what job is the word doing in this sentence?
explain: Look at phrases like «mosquito net» and «mosquito repellent». The phrase has its own meaning: a net keeps mosquitoes off you while you sleep, and repellent is a spray or cream that stops them biting.
fact: A mosquito is a small flying insect with long legs.
fact: Only female mosquitoes bite, because they need blood to make their eggs.
fact: Male mosquitoes do not bite; they drink plant juice instead.
fact: Mosquitoes lay their eggs in still water, and their young, called larvae, live in the water too.
fact: «Mosquito bite» means the itchy bump left on your skin after a mosquito has bitten you.
exercise: «Spiders in homes eat flies, mosquitoes and other pests.» In this sentence, what are mosquitoes? | Large birds that eat spiders | *Food for spiders | Spiders' homes | Flowers that grow in the house
exercise: Which mosquitoes bite people and animals? | *Only the females | All mosquitoes, male and female | Only the males | None of them
exercise: What does a «mosquito net» do? | It turns mosquitoes into flies | It is a kind of bed made of wood | *It keeps mosquitoes off people while they sleep | It catches fish in rivers
test: Where do mosquitoes lay their eggs? | High up in the tops of trees | *In still water | Inside people's blood | In hot, dry sand
test: Which of these helps stop mosquito bites? | Sleeping with no net and the windows wide open | *Using repellent and wearing long sleeves | Leaving standing water in buckets | Going out in shorts with no spray
exam: The sentence «the mosquito biting your arm is, for people, the deadliest animal of all» suggests that the word deadliest means | *They can be very dangerous to people | They are the biggest animal in the world | They are friendly pets that people like | They only eat plants
